over the weekend bitcoin's price crashed  aggressively and there was a Cascade of  liquidations across the market now a lot  of people are wondering why is Bitcoin  crashing given the global macro  environment wasn't Bitcoin supposed to  be an inflation hedge what exactly is  happening in these portfolios but  there's a key thing to remember yes  bitcoin's correlation to other assets  including the S P 500 hitting an  all-time high right now Bitcoin and the  S P 500 a correlation of 0.6 now of  course up until 2020 there was no  correlation at all between Bitcoin and  other assets it was a non-correlated  asset but once the institution started  to come in and they started to adopt  Bitcoin and put it in their portfolio  now all of a sudden they treat Bitcoin  as the most risky asset in their  portfolio if the global macro  environment calls for risk off well  guess what the institutions do they sell  those assets they go back to value  stocks or some sort of commodity in  which they feel is less risky now of  course the Institute tuitions act  completely differently than the retail  investors who are simply dollar cost  averaging into Bitcoin they continue to  accumulate more regardless of price but  we can go all the way back to 2008 and  2009 to get a little bit of History to  understand how correlations and  liquidity crisis play out here you can  see the gold price chart back in 2007  2008 and 2009. you can see that over the  summer of 2008 gold went down 30 percent  that liquidity crisis of the 2008 Global  financial crisis meant that all asset  correlations trended towards one even  though many people would accept the fact  that gold served as a safe haven or an  inflation hedge asset it still was not  immune to the liquidity crisis that was  at play and so if you fast forward back  to 2022 we're in a liquidity crisis  right now it's not nearly as severe as  March of 2020 which was highly acute and  happened very quickly instead we've been  in a liquidity crisis since the end of  last year and now we're about eight  months into this and as the FED  continues to raise interest rates and  conduct quantitative tightening they  simply are forcing investors to sell any  asset that they can and raise cash the  US dollar is at a 20-year High  relatively compared to other Fiat  currencies but what you as an investor  need to understand is that liquidity  crisis they eventually go away and  correlations will return back to  something like where they were before  the liquidity crisis and so yes Bitcoin  and all other assets are going down  a global 60 40 portfolio filled with  stocks and bonds is down normally those  would have an inverse relationship  stocks go up bonds go down or vice versa  but that's not what we're seeing in this  current liquidity crisis that has lasted  more than six months all asset prices  are going down Bitcoin is not immune and  neither is any other asset class so  understanding how these types of assets  and liquidity crises interact is really  important Bitcoin and the S P 500  hitting an all-time high correlation  something tells me it won't stay here  over the long run but it's still  important to understand what's happening  today and try to figure out how you are  going to move your portfolio to be able  to protect yourself and or benefit on  the other side
 

